Both full 10M source passes completed. The first scoring implementation then filtered
the entire selected-history table once per query, creating avoidable quadratic work.
It was cancelled before any summary was produced. The corrected implementation groups
outgoing and reverse histories once, then scores each query inside its exact group.

The first grouped correction also materialized a DataFrame for every selected pair,
which caused memory pressure. It too was cancelled without output. The final version
stores compact positional group indices and only groups reverse pairs actually queried.
